Third-party components
----------------------
This image includes the third-party programs below. Each keeps its own
license. Deadfin runs ffmpeg and ffprobe as separate processes.

* jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.1-1 (package jellyfin-ffmpeg8, installed in
  /usr/lib/jellyfin-ffmpeg)
  The Jellyfin project's build of FFmpeg. It is configured with
  --enable-gpl --enable-version3, so the binaries are licensed under the
  GNU General Public License, version 3 or later. `ffmpeg -L` prints the
  license.
  License and copyright: /usr/share/doc/jellyfin-ffmpeg8/copyright
  GPL-3 text: /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3
  Corresponding source (release v8.1.1-1, with the build scripts and
  patches):
    https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/releases/tag/v8.1.1-1
    https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/tree/v8.1.1-1

* libvips (Debian bookworm packages libvips42 and libvips-tools)
  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.
  License and copyright: /usr/share/doc/libvips42/copyright
  LGPL-2.1 text: /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1
  Source: https://sources.debian.org/src/vips/ (the version is in
  `dpkg -s libvips42`)

* SkiaSharp 3.119.4 native library (/usr/local/lib/deadfin/libSkiaSharp.so)
  MIT License, with bundled third-party notices.
  /usr/share/licenses/skia-sharp/3.119.4/
  Source: https://www.nuget.org/packages/SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux/3.119.4
  (https://github.com/mono/SkiaSharp)

* Other Debian packages (the base image, ca-certificates, the libraries
  that libvips and jellyfin-ffmpeg depend on, and intel-opencl-icd on amd64)
  Each package's license is in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright. Source
  for each package is at https://sources.debian.org/ (the versions are in
  `dpkg -l`).

Written offer
-------------
For at least three years after we last distribute a given image, the
Deadfin maintainers will give any third party, on request, a complete
machine-readable copy of the corresponding source code of every GPL and LGPL
component in that image, for a charge no more than the cost of physically
performing the distribution. Ask through an issue at
https://github.com/deadfin-org/deadfin/issues and name the image digest.
